From 7a03f91449db70f970d5bfde4b9a708074b5d802 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gavin John <gavinnjohn@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 04:50:54 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 73/97] packetizer: mpeg4audio: let a break cost one frame, not
 the rest of the block

Same as the mpeg audio packetizer: what is left of a block once a frame has
been taken out of it goes back to the caller and comes straight back here,
still flagged, and the second reset arrives with the block's timestamp already
spent, so the rest of the block is dropped.

Measured on a 4 s aac item in a transport stream looped with --repeat on a
null sink, silence per loop in the capture: 0.245-0.250 s -> 0.035 s, and the
60 ms marker at the head of each pass, which had been swallowed whole, is
heard on all four passes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 modules/packetizer/mpeg4audio.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/modules/packetizer/mpeg4audio.c b/modules/packetizer/mpeg4audio.c
index 72d91b5b2d..4bade545fe 100644
--- a/modules/packetizer/mpeg4audio.c
+++ b/modules/packetizer/mpeg4audio.c
@@ -1269,6 +1269,11 @@ static block_t *Packetize(decoder_t *p_dec, block_t **pp_block)
                 block_Release(p_block);
                 return NULL;
             }
+
+            /* What is left of this block once a frame has been taken out of
+             * it comes straight back here, and the break belongs to the seam
+             * the block arrived on, not to the rest of the block. */
+            p_block->i_flags &= ~BLOCK_FLAG_DISCONTINUITY;
         }
 
         if (!date_Get(&p_sys->end_date) && p_block->i_pts <= VLC_TICK_INVALID)
